 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2021-04-19",
   "text": "Climate Risk Disclosure Act of 2021\n This bill directs the Securities and Exchange Commission to require an issuer of securities to annually disclose information regarding climate change-related risks posed to the issuer, including an issuer's strategies and actions to mitigate these risks.\n Specifically, issuers must report their direct and indirect greenhouse-gas emissions and disclose their fossil fuel-related assets."
  }
 ],
